<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wibald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1098–1158</span> · Also known as Wibald of Stavelot, Wibald of Corvey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wibald was abbot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavelot">Stavelot</a> from 1130 and also of Corvey from 1146, and one of the leading statesmen of 12th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He advised the emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a> III, Conrad III and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, and his collected letters are an important historical source. He commissioned fine Mosan metalwork for Stavelot and died while on an embassy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>.</p></div>
